(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #114, the boolean cast direction: a boolean value
 stored under a dynamically-set key, read into a `number` slot (0/1, the
 language's own representation) and into a `text` slot ("true"/"false"),
 exactly as an explicit `as a number` / `as a text` would.)

a map called flags is {}.
Set flags's "on" to true.
a number called n is flags's "on".
Print "{n}".
a text called t is flags's "on".
Print "{t}".
